config BR2_PACKAGE_USB_CDC
	bool "USB CDC ACM data-port example"
	help
	  Configure the STM32F429 Discovery USB USER connector as a CDC ACM
	  serial device. The connector uses the OTG HS controller's internal
	  full-speed PHY. On the host it normally appears as /dev/ttyACM0;
	  on the board it is /dev/ttyGS0.

	  USART1 remains the Linux console. Use ttyGS0 as an independent data
	  port for manual transfers or run usb-cdc to echo host data back.
	  Connect the host to the board's USB USER micro-AB connector, not the
	  ST-LINK USB connector.
